@startuml
title Splunk Operator — PostgreSQL Lifecycle State Machines

skinparam StateBackgroundColor #E0F2FE
skinparam StateBorderColor #0284C7
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7F9FC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #64748B

state "PostgresCluster phase" as Cluster {
  [*] --> Pending
  Pending : upstream inputs not yet present\n(class, secret, empty CNPG phase);\nCNPG FailOver in progress
  Provisioning : CNPG FirstPrimary / CreatingReplica;\ncomponent still creating (e.g. pooler)
  Configuring : CNPG Switchover / Upgrade /\nApplyingConfiguration / Restart / Promotion
  Ready : all components Ready +\nCNPG Healthy
  Failed : CNPG Unrecoverable / WaitingForUser /\nplugin or image error; build/patch failed

  Pending --> Provisioning : inputs published
  Provisioning --> Configuring : CNPG applies change
  Provisioning --> Ready : all components converge
  Configuring --> Ready : change complete
  Ready --> Configuring : spec change / CNPG switchover
  Ready --> Provisioning : replica rebuild
  Provisioning --> Failed : unrecoverable
  Configuring --> Failed : unrecoverable
  Ready --> Failed : CNPG regresses
  Failed --> Configuring : manual intervention resolves
}

note right of Cluster
  Phase is projected from the CNPG
  Cluster phase; only the top-level
  reconciler declares Ready, and only
  once every component observes Ready.
end note

state "PostgresDatabase phase" as Database {
  [*] --> PendingDB
  PendingDB : cluster not found / not Ready\n(ClusterReady=False)
  ProvisioningDB : secrets, configMaps, roles,\ndatabases being reconciled
  ReadyDB : phase set once DatabasesReady=True;\nprivilege grants run after,\ncan leave PrivilegesReady=False while still ReadyDB
  FailedDB : role conflict / role reconcile failed
  DeletingDB : deletion in progress\n(finalizer draining)

  PendingDB --> ProvisioningDB : cluster Ready
  ProvisioningDB --> ReadyDB : DatabasesReady=True\n(privilege grants follow, may lag)
  ProvisioningDB --> FailedDB : role conflict / failure
  ProvisioningDB --> PendingDB : cluster regresses
  ReadyDB --> ProvisioningDB : spec change / drift
  ReadyDB --> PendingDB : cluster regresses
  FailedDB --> ProvisioningDB : conflict resolved
  ReadyDB --> DeletingDB : deletionTimestamp set
  ProvisioningDB --> DeletingDB : deletionTimestamp set
  DeletingDB --> [*] : finalizer removed\n(Delete drops, Retain orphans)
}

note right of Database
  Linear pipeline accumulates conditions:
  ClusterReady -> SecretsReady ->
  ConfigMapsReady -> RolesReady ->
  DatabasesReady -> PrivilegesReady.
  Phase is set to ReadyDB at the DatabasesReady
  step, one step before PrivilegesReady — a
  superuser secret fetch failure in that last
  step can leave phase ReadyDB with
  PrivilegesReady still False.
end note
@enduml
